" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486367 #edb/ref 1074 "The additive inverse of a number is the number that lies at the same distance from zero on the number line, but on the opposite side. \n\nAs we can see on the number line below, the distance of $-2$ from zero is $2$ units. The only other number that is at a distance of $2$ units from zero is $2.$\n\n![](images/03/035ad7581b3084ab33917ceb4560b46054871f96551b30825d5c14239a7c0687.png)\n\nTherefore, the additive inverse of $-2$ is $2$, and it can be represented on the number line as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75b5ed5f417e89d2ed58f5b2892f43bdbf64ca44da2e7b031a18a9147fd2940a.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357007" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $p=-6$ and $q=9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e975e85-092f-5a1a-be8e-b7301eb722e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486377 #edb/ref 1074 "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=-6$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=9$, so the distance we move is $|q|=9.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $9$ units to the *right* from $-6.$\n\n![](images/17/17c56561e34f16a80df8ee8872401f7a3df4930c28c38ce70c1dcf202269f3d0.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-6+9=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1069 "q-356985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $u=4$ and $v=-9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $u+v?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5daaab8a-c401-527b-849d-4cd75e79ca94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486390 #edb/ref 1074 "The value of $u+v$ is the number located a distance $|v|$ from $u$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $v$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $v$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $u=4$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $v=-9$, so the distance we move is $|v|=9.$\n\n- Because $v$ is *negative*, we move $9$ units to the *left* from $4.$\n\n![](images/79/79c5200c6f0089f7b6cf6be0eec8b97de3ff3a3daa270bfa6e7ae0c480b134f5.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n4+(-9)=-5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486281 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1069 "q-356966" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1071 "A bank account had an **initial balance** of $$0.$ During the day, there was a **deposit** of $$20.$ Then there was a **withdrawal** of $$20$ later.\nWhat is the resulting amount in the account?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae45fb99-3296-59e3-8a59-381f72003cfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486426 #edb/ref 1074 "In our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *deposit of* $$20,$ which is a change of $+$20.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *withdrawal of* $$20,$ which is a change of $-$20.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n20+(-20)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $$0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357009" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $p=1$ and $q=-6.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2201c29-9c53-5378-91b2-19915c1b3e60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486429 #edb/ref 1074 "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p=1$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q=-6$, so the distance we move is $|q|=6.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *negative*, we move $6$ units to the *left* from $1.$\n\n![](images/f4/f488d1dc3787fefc588e143e7808fee7e4473a9918986b49bc36344e6a153b25.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n1+(-6)=-5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486432 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22721" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486432 #edb/ref 1071 "A drone’s elevation **dropped by** $85\\text{ m}$ while descending into a valley. Then it **rose by** $85\\text{ m}$ while flying back up.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The drone’s elevation is now higher than the initial elevation.\n\nII. The drone’s elevation is now lower than the initial elevation.\n\nIII. The drone returned to the initial elevation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b716c849-40fa-5f39-a344-ee1a0ebde20d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486432 #edb/ref 1074 "In our situation:\n\n- While descending, the drone’s elevation *dropped by* $85\\text{ m}$, which is a change of $-85\\text{ m}.$\n\n- While climbing back up, the drone’s elevation *rose by* $85\\text{ m},$ which is a change of $+85\\text{ m}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-85 + 85 = 0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total elevation change* is $0\\text{ m},$ so the drone returns to the original elevation.\n\nSo, statements I and II are false, while statement III is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1069 "q-357097" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1071 "The temperature inside an oven **dropped by** ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ when the door was opened. Then it **rose by** ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ when the door was closed.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The temperature is now lower than the initial value.\n\nII. The temperature returned to the initial value.\n\nIII. The temperature is now larger than the initial value." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "caba3d37-19c8-51f8-9627-60834d1806c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486442 #edb/ref 1074 "In our situation:\n\n- When the door was opened, the temperature *dropped by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, which is a change of $-{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\n- When the door was closed, the temperature *rose by* ${25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ which is a change of $+{25}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n-25+25=0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total temperature change* is ${0}^{∘}\\,\\text{C},$ so the temperature returns to its original value.\n\nSo, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486449 #edb/ref 1069 "e-22722" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486449 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $p=-3$ and $q=8.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486449 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d5c1d845-4926-5b71-9aaf-b7f1a7983af3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486449 #edb/ref 1074 "The value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p = -3$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q = 8$, so the distance we move is $|q| = 8.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *positive*, we move $8$ units to the *right* from $-3.$\n\n![](images/b4/b44a40ef3278f0b31899b7a98695a92e332859b5d0f7badb82a241b1bcbef022.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-3 + 8 = 5.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1071 "On which number line does the red dot represent the additive inverse of $5?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ed0dc0e5-67a3-5514-ad15-795a9dd0dc11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486454 #edb/ref 1074 "The only two numbers that are at a distance of $5$ from zero are $5$ and $-5.$ So, $-5$ is the additive inverse of $5.$\n\n![](images/4c/4cdd56412bb16297332f16cf977cd6314c6f885460bf270418e010ed728f19a6.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\n![](images/49/4986262570b7133149b8b709c64127873d5c1a90ef642c45e7b97850808dfb82.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1069 "q-356997" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1071 "A drone’s elevation **rose by** $85\\text{ m}$ while flying up to a roof. Then it **dropped by** $85\\text{ m}$ while descending back to the pilot.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The drone's elevation is now higher than the initial elevation.\n\nII. The drone returned to the initial elevation.\n\nIII. The drone's elevation is now lower than the initial elevation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef66e122-a2b4-5616-86af-6621c724508e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486455 #edb/ref 1074 "In our situation:\n\n- While flying up to a roof, the drone’s elevation *rose by* $85\\text{ m}$, which is a change of $+85\\text{ m}.$\n\n- While descending back to the pilot, the drone’s elevation *dropped by* $85\\text{ m},$ which is a change of $-85\\text{ m}.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0:$\n\n$$\n85+(-85)=0\n$$\n\nThis means the *total elevation change* is $0\\text{ m},$ so the drone returns to the original elevation.\n\nSo, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186486303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1069 "q-356982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $x=-5$ and $y=8.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $x+y?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe75ee40-dd66-5b6a-be0b-41d26c4e980f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486462 #edb/ref 1074 "The value of $x+y$ is the number located a distance $|y|$ from $x$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $y$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $y$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $x=-5$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $y=8$, so the distance we move is $|y|=8.$\n\n- Because $y$ is *positive*, we move $8$ units to the *right* from $-5.$\n\n![](images/6f/6f3852a3695e81aa36441b6e579cce31c337aa81aa5af8ee2944bdcce7fb76d3.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n-5+8=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486468 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486468 #edb/ref 1061 621965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486468 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "160c60e9-5ab9-50b5-945e-8198d95f11e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486468 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486474 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486474 #edb/ref 1061 621964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486474 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "31b8f5ad-d1ac-5b65-a264-059708293d82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486474 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486476 #edb/ref 1061 621975 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486476 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "44f3d1e3-06b3-5448-ac19-3aaeecc7c475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486476 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486496 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486496 #edb/ref 1061 621974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486496 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "903b1e70-5068-5da3-8e39-2277b886461a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486496 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486498 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486498 #edb/ref 1061 621970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486498 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "93b60de0-a7f7-5e60-b050-2b523dabb82e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486498 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486500 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186486498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486500 #edb/ref 1061 621969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486500 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9f48a277-1ef5-5804-98e6-8970d7e2ee30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486500 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186486526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486524 #edb/ref 1064 "On a number line, a number and its *additive inverse* are at the same distance from zero but on opposite sides. Remember that the distance of a number from zero is given by its *absolute value*.\n\nFor instance, the only two numbers that are at a distance of $4$ from zero are $4$ and $-4.$ So, $-4$ is the additive inverse of $4$ (and vice versa).\n\n![](images/c0/c0ac86b7f6b42079f164e07e9c0f7c8e35589c1eb8b1fe8762094ff1a59d0d5c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486524 #edb/ref 1065 15163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486524 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d29afdb4-83a8-5d44-85aa-588cb62c58d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486524 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486525 #edb/ref 1064 "Now, let $p=6$ and $q=-9.$ What point on the number line corresponds to $p+q?$\n\nThe value of $p+q$ is the number located a distance $|q|$ from $p$ on the number line, \n\n- moving to the *right* if $q$ is *positive*, and\n\n- moving to the *left* if $q$ is *negative*.\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- We start at $p = 6$ on the number line.\n\n- Here, $q = -9$, so the distance we move is $|q| = 9.$\n\n- Because $q$ is *negative*, we move $9$ units to the *left* from $6.$\n\n![](images/26/265469a65efa2ae63d794ee2ad0eeb79c6754ab18a7bec3791b8ba05007a744e.png)\n\nThis point corresponds to the number\n\n$$\n6 + (-9) = -3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486525 #edb/ref 1065 15173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486525 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e93c19c4-c6b0-531d-b9a0-f2a16df8a410" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486525 #edb/ref 1067 "Addition and Absolute Values on the Number Line" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486526 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that a bank account had an *initial balance* of $\\[math]0.$ During the day, there was a *withdrawal* of $\\[/math]80.$ Then there was a *deposit* of $\\[math]80$ later.  \n\nWhat is the resulting amount in the account?\n\nIn our situation:\n\n- During the day, the account had a *withdrawal of* $\\[/math]80,$ which is a change of $-\\[math]80.$\n\n- Later, the account had a *deposit of* $\\[/math]80,$ which is a change of $+\\[math]80.$\n\nThese two changes are *opposite quantities*. When opposite quantities combine, they make $0{:}$\n\n$$\n-80 + 80 = 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance returns to its original value of $\\[/math]0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486526 #edb/ref 1065 15172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486526 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f0d64651-a1e2-53b0-889b-8b5a7d8cddd6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186486526 #edb/ref 1067 "Opposite Quantities Combine to Zero" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
